  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday morning through next Saturday)\nIssued at 226 PM EDT Sun Sep 27 2026\n\nPleasant conditions will continue through the work week. \nTemperatures in the upper 80s and lower 90s for much of the CWA as \nthe high pressure begins to break down and winds become more \nsoutherly in the second half of the week. \n\nAs we approach the weekend, the ridge will begin to break down and \nsoutherly flow will begin to pull moisture back into the CWA. This \nwill bring chances for thunderstorms back up to between 25-35% \nduring the afternoon on Friday with more widespread thunderstorms \nlikely through the weekend. Temperatures should remain moderated to \nthe upper 80s and lower 90s, though that still has them running 5-10 \ndegrees above normal for this time of year. \n\nWe'll need to keep an eye on Sunday, as the best dynamics move \nthrough the area for stronger thunderstorms. The ECMWF builds in \nplenty of instability and decent low level shear, though the GFS \ntends to keep a majority of the bulk shear off to the north.",
